# Take the feat a menu longer than the alphabet used to hide: inc-ysa.
#
# A Wood Elf Druid at seed 7 is offered 88 feats. TextTerm::LMenu draws a
# selection letter beside each one, and it has 52 to give (a-z then A-Z), so
# 36 of those feats used to be drawn "[ ]" and no keypress could name them.
# Natural Aptitude was one of them.
#
# WHY THIS CHARACTER. Metamagic is what pushes the list past the alphabet, so
# a full spellcaster is the shortest route to the defect; a fighter's list is
# short enough to fit. A druid also gets his feats at first level, before any
# levelling is needed, and Natural Aptitude asks a second question -- "Choose
# a skill:" -- which proves the menu really returned that feat and not its
# neighbour.
#
# WHAT MAKES IT AN ORACLE. @choose reads the letter the game has just printed
# beside the name and presses it. On a build with the defect there is no
# letter to read, so @choose refuses and the run ends with exit 6. It cannot
# quietly press the wrong key and pass.
#
# TAB is the page key. It exists only on a menu that overflows, and @until
# sends it no more than it must: on a build with the defect the name is
# already on screen (all 88 are drawn, 36 of them unselectable) so no TAB is
# sent at all, and the failure that follows is the missing letter and nothing
# else.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes

@choose "Elf"
@choose "Wood Elf"
@choose "Druid"
a       # Attributes: the first of the offered sets
e       # Alignment: [e] Neutral. Nine fixed entries, so the letter is safe,
        #   and "Neutral" by name would match four of them.

@expect "Choose a feat"
@until "Natural Aptitud" TAB     # the menu truncates the name to the column
@choose "Natural Aptitude"
@expect "Choose a skill"
@choose "Alchemy"                # a skill no druid carries, so the sheet
                                 #   showing it is the feat having worked

@while "Choose a feat" a         # whatever else the class asks for
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y                          # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks
a                                # Personality archetype
@while "Choose a feat" a
a a a a                          # starting spells

@until "Entry Chamber" ESC       # in play
d                                # character sheet
@until "Natural Aptitude" PGDN   # scroll to the Feats block
@dump:sheet-feats
ESC
@quit
